[36m(RolloutManager pid=30971)[0m [2026-09-29 06:45:12.294 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:473 - First rollout sample: ['<|im_start|>user\nThe profit from a business transaction is shared among 2 business partners, Mike and Johnson in the ratio 2:5 respectively. If Johnson got $2500, how much will Mike have after spending some of his share on a shirt that costs $200?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nWe are given:\n\n- The profit **shares** of Mike and Johnson are in the ratio **2:5**.\n- Johnson gets **$2500**.\n- We are to find **how much Mike will have after spending some of his share on a shirt that costs **$200**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Set up variables\n\nLet the total profit be divided between Mike and Johnson in the ratio **2:5**. So:\n\n- Mike’s share : Johnson’s share = 2 : 5  \n- So, total profit = 7 parts (2 + 5)\n\nJohnson’s share is 5 parts, and we are told he gets $2500.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the value of each part\n\n$$\n\\text{Value of 1 part} = \\frac{2500}{5} = 500\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n- Mike’s share = 2 × 500 = $1000  \n- Johnson’s share = 5 × 500 = $2500 ✅\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Determine how much Mike will have after spending on the shirt\n\nThe shirt costs **$200**, so he spends this money on it.\n\n$$\n\\text{Mike’s final amount} = \\text{Mike’s original share} - \\text{amount spent on shirt}\n= 1000 - 200 = \\boxed{800}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{800}\n$$<|im_end|>'], label: 800, reward: 1.0
